  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Return and Sustainable Reintegration for Victims of Trafficking and Foreign Citizens in Prostitution in Sweden (RRTiPP-SWE) 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this project is to support foreign citizens in Sweden who have been identified as victims or presumed victims of human trafficking or exploitation, including in prostitution, through a rights-based approach to return safely and in dignity, and to achieve sustainable reintegration. The programme contributes to the Government of Sweden&#x2019;s action plan to counter trafficking in persons. During this programme phase, it is estimated that approximately 120 presumed victims of human trafficking or exploitation will be supported. This will include supporting counterparts in providing initial counselling to approximately 45 potential new beneficiaries, out of which approximately 5 are estimated to receive IOM&#x2019;s return and reintegration assistance and 10 are estimated to receive reintegration assistance. The programme will also continue supporting an estimated number of 75 beneficiaries who have returned during previous programme phases and where the reintegration process is still ongoing. The support is delivered in close cooperation with stakeholders in Sweden and countries of return.</narrative>
  </description>
